{"id":10888,"date":"2024-01-11T17:05:22","date_gmt":"2024-01-12T01:05:22","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=10888"},"modified":"2024-10-29T12:15:23","modified_gmt":"2024-10-29T19:15:23","slug":"0-2-before-you-fly-jrotc","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-2-before-you-fly-jrotc\/","title":{"rendered":"0.2 Before You Fly (JROTC ed.)"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213092d86c\" name=\"6a2213092d86c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Before Flying<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1730229169902{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-11766 alignleft\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"106\" height=\"107\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>PRE-FLIGHT WARNING<\/strong><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\">Our drones are durable, yet not indestructible. Please exercise caution while piloting your drone. To prolong the longevity of your drone, avoid flying into walls or other objects.<\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]A good pilot always checks their environment, performs an inspection of the hardware, and reviews the safety rules and recommendations before even turning on the drone.\u00a0 Watch the safety video below and then proceed to the flight checks.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Note: Although CoDrone EDU (JROTC ed.) may be a different color, all the information presented in this video still applies.<\/strong>[\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/youtu.be\/Fzbb9EERsZo&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221; title=&#8221;Safety with CoDrone EDU&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213092d9c0\" name=\"6a2213092d9c0\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Check Your Environment<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<strong>Fly Indoors<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>CoDrone EDU (JROTC ed.) is designed for indoor flight only. This means no flying outside! The drone is not built to withstand strong winds or other weather patterns. There are also <a href=\"https:\/\/robolink.helpdocs.io\/article\/bgd5cv350b-is-the-co-drone-edu-faa-compliant\">certain rules<\/a> to follow when piloting a drone outside. If you don&#8217;t follow those rules, it can be a safety hazard for you and others. For these reasons, keep your drone indoors.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10951&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<strong>Clear Out Obstacles<\/strong><\/p>\n<div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 4\">\n<div class=\"layoutArea\">\n<div class=\"column\">\n<p>Find an open area for flight without obstacles. Put away anything fragile or open liquids you do not want knocked over!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9489&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<strong>Maintain a Safe Flight Height<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>CoDrone EDU (JROTC ed.) can be damaged by any falls or crashes higher than 10 feet. It is recommended to stay in an environment with lower ceilings, as opposed to gymnasiums or large auditoriums. If this is not possible, pilots should be cautious to stay within safe flight heights.<\/p>\n<h3><\/h3>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9596&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<strong>Check Connectivity Strength<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Radio frequency is obstructed by walls, especially glass or metal ones. Water will also obstruct signal strength (this means people too!). For best connectivity, make sure you have enough space to aim the controller directly at the drone.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9491&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<strong>Find the Best Floor for Flying<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The optical flow sensor on CoDrone EDU (JROTC ed.) works best with a patterned floor that is well-lit. If CoDrone EDU (JROTC ed.) is drifting uncontrollably during flight, try flying over a different material.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9597&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213092da18\" name=\"6a2213092da18\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Check Your Drone<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Take your drone out of the box. Without powering the drone on, check the following to make sure your drone is in the proper condition for flying. If the drone is not in proper condition, it can cause a failure in flight that can damage your drone.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9598&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213092da6e\" name=\"6a2213092da6e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Flight Rules<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The following rules and best practices should be kept anytime you are using your drone. It is the safe and responsible way to fly. We will review these rules one more time before your first flight![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9601&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221;][vc_column_text]<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-medium wp-image-11766 alignleft\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"84\" height=\"85\" \/>If your drone motor stalls during takeoff and is not spinning, <strong>immediately\u00a0<\/strong>emergency stop the motors to prevent motor burnout.<\/p>\n<p>Once stopped, please review the information found in our Help Docs article &#8220;<a href=\"https:\/\/robolink.helpdocs.io\/article\/7o1560fbai-what-do-i-do-if-one-of-my-co-drone-edu-propellers-isn-t-spinning\">What do I do if one of my CoDrone EDU propellers isn&#8217;t spinning<\/a>?&#8221;[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213092dabd\" name=\"6a2213092dabd\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Label Your Drone<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]If your drone and controller do not already have labels, we&#8217;ve included a set of stickers for you to use. Label your drone and controller with the same label so you can keep them together for future flights.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Note:<\/strong> If you are in a classroom or your drones already have labels on them, make sure to ask your teacher or coach before re-labeling any drones.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9603&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213092db17\" name=\"6a2213092db17\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Check Your Firmware<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Occasionally there are firmware updates for your CoDrone EDU (JROTC ed.) drone or controller. Periodically check that your hardware is up-to-date, especially if this is your first time using the drone.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Note: The firmware for CoDrone EDU (JROTC ed.) is not the same as CoDrone EDU.<\/strong>[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]<a href=\"https:\/\/robolink.helpdocs.io\/article\/d8zr66v6fj-codrone-edu-jrotc-drone-firmware\">Instructions for updating the drone<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/robolink.helpdocs.io\/article\/ylrsovzws2-codrone-edu-jrotc-controller-firmware\">Instruction for updating the controller<\/a>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213092db72\" name=\"6a2213092db72\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Review<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Did you complete this checklist? Let&#8217;s review:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check your environment<\/li>\n<li>Check your drone for any damages before flying<\/li>\n<li>Study the rules of operation<\/li>\n<li>Label the drone and controller together<\/li>\n<li>Check firmware<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>Whenever you are about to fly, make sure to go through each item above again. In the next lesson, you will learn all about the drone and controller hardware and how to maintain them.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 8 Before Flying [vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1730229169902{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}\"] PRE-FLIGHT WARNING Our drones are durable, yet not indestructible. Please exercise&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-2-before-you-fly-jrotc\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":11245,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"easy","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":10878,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[14401,8415,10471,8419,8417,2214],"class_list":["post-10888","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-cdej","lesson-tag-checklist","lesson-tag-jrotc-ed","lesson-tag-rules","lesson-tag-safety","lesson-tag-setup","module-getting-started","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/10888","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":28,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/10888\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":13063,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/10888\/revisions\/13063"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/11245"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=10888"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=10888"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=10888"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}